From: Ed Maros <ed.maros@ligo.org>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] framecpp/test/CMakeLists: guard test_verify_options add_test
 blocks against missing target on cross-compile arches

The framecpp_target_executable() helper at test/CMakeLists.txt:52
early-returns on some cross-compile scenarios, so the test_verify_options
target may not be created — but the add_test() calls that reference
$<TARGET_FILE:test_verify_options> did not have a matching guard, so
CMake configure failed with

    CMake Error at test/CMakeLists.txt:650 (add_test):
      Error evaluating generator expression:
        $<TARGET_FILE:test_verify_options>
      No target "test_verify_options"

on conda-forge's linux_aarch64 and linux_ppc64le cross-compile-with-qemu
builds (native builds and osx cross-compile arches are unaffected).

Wrap both add_test() blocks with `AND TARGET test_verify_options`, matching
the guard pattern already used elsewhere in this file (e.g. the
`if(TARGET framecpp_checksum)` block added for #390/#400).

Filed upstream as https://git.ligo.org/computing/ldastools/LDAS_Tools/-/issues/405.
---
 test/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/CMakeLists.txt b/test/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@ endif()
 ##-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Phase 0: Baseline test with all Verify options disabled
 # This establishes that minimal frames are valid and pass with no validation
-if(BUILD_TESTING)
+if(BUILD_TESTING AND TARGET test_verify_options)
   add_test(
     NAME verify_phase0_baseline_all_disabled
     COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:test_verify_options>
@@ -678,7 +678,7 @@ set(VERIFY_OPTIONS
   CollectAllErrors
 )

-if(BUILD_TESTING)
+if(BUILD_TESTING AND TARGET test_verify_options)
   foreach(option IN LISTS VERIFY_OPTIONS)
     add_test(
       NAME verify_phase1_${option}
